> As a general rule I am for using scientific notation and 4 to 6
> significant digits (e.g. 0.123456E-20). This may be my FORTRAN
> background though :)

That seems too precise, given that most imput dosages/probabilities are
known to ~3 or 4 digits and I don't think that many phenotypes will be
measured more precisely.

> 
> What if we decide to put say p-values in the outputs? Does the output
> automatically switch to sci notation in this case? 

For p-values I would definitely go for scientific notation. We can turn
the on/off per output column (as each column is coded as a stringstream).


Lennart.

